[I think I may have skimmed a message that answered this, but on re-searching
recent messages I can't find it, so maybe I imagined the answer when I
first skimmed Nick's message...]

Separate ce'u have to be independent variables. {ce'u prami ce'u} cannot
mean "self-love" -- that would be {ce'u prami loi nei}. But at the
same time, {ko'a prami loi nei} is an instance of {ce'u xi pa prami 
ce'u xi re}, and if you want to define the property of loving something
other than oneself, then this would have to be {ce'u prami lo na nei
no'u ce'u} or somesuch.

